    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "A theatre has 500 seats. When tickets are priced at $\\$20$, all seats are sold.\nFor each $\\$2$ increase in price, 25 fewer tickets are sold. Let $x$ be the number of $\\$2$ increases.\nShow that the total revenue is $R=10000+500x-50x^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$R=(20+2x)(500-25x)=10000+500x-50x^2$ dollars.",
